Thu Sep 18 00:00:00 UTC 2026 - Ronald Pina <rpina@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.7.1
  + Cloud metadata: the instance-metadata alias every cloud instance
    carries in /etc/hosts (169.254.169.254 metadata.google.internal
    metadata) is no longer learned as a hostname, so
    public_cloud/metadata.txt keeps its name instead of arriving as
    hostname_N.txt; names on that address are aliases of one service,
    not hosts, and the exclusion is case-insensitive. A customer host
    whose name merely starts with metadata is still obfuscated
  + Renaming a file or directory now applies exactly the scrubbers the
    file CONTENT gets, in the same order, instead of a plain substring
    replace: a host called work no longer turns network.txt into
    nethostname_N.txt, a host called mess no longer cuts messages.txt
    in half, and a name that differs only in case is renamed like the
    text is
  + hostname_preserve from the configuration now reaches every entry
    point. It was honoured in the parallel path alone, so in a default
    run the documented "never obfuscated" names were obfuscated anyway;
    a preserved name is also never given a mapping, however it arrives
    (harvest, --hostname, or an older mapping file)
  + Every rename is reported: a count on each run, the old and new name
    of each with --verbose, and the pairs in the --report JSON. A file
    that changed name silently read as a file the tool had lost
  + Empty directories in the source are kept in the scrubbed output
    (public_cloud/regcache), while the archive's own wrapper directory
    is not recreated inside it

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Sep 16 00:00:00 UTC 2026 - Ronald Pina <rpina@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.7
  + Credentials: mask command-line secrets (--password, --passphrase,
    credentials=), URL logins and HTTP Basic credentials, and the
    name/value attribute form with a wider secret charset; verify
    checks for the same forms
  + Hostnames: learn cluster members from the cluster's own membership
    records (CIB node table, crm_mon, corosync nodelist) and adopted
    node names from the tree structure (crm_report node dirs, nested
    supportconfigs); preserved names restored in one regex pass
  + New --preload: learn names from every input of a case, write the
    shared mapping, and scrub nothing, so each per-capture scrub starts
    with the complete name set
  + Compressed single-file logs: every .gz/.xz/.bz2 rewrite is read
    back and validated as a complete stream before it replaces the
    original; a file whose extension does not match its content is
    scrubbed as plain text and the extension dropped; non-text payloads
    left byte-identical; truncated streams salvaged and rewritten;
    invalid UTF-8 bytes survive the round trip; leftover mismatches
    reported on every run; verify no longer skips a compressed file
    it cannot decompress
  + Compressed logs scrubbed in bounded segments, file mode included,
    so peak memory no longer grows with the decompressed size
  + Binary files under plain names (packet captures, core dumps,
    images) left unchanged and reported instead of rewritten as text
  + Domains: file names such as pam_unix.so, libc.so or omsutil.py are
    no longer learned as domains and renamed
  + Deterministic output: files walked in sorted order and a domain map
    tie-break independent of the hash seed, so a mapping depends only
    on the content
  + Parallel fakes keyed per run; the key is kept in the mapping file,
    never in output, and --mappings reuses it
  + Audit log: values passed with --hostname, --domain, --username,
    --keywords, --keyword-file and --mappings are redacted
  + Folder mode: several directories in one run share one pool and one
    mapping
  + File mode scrubs serials and SIDs like every other input mode
  + Performance: longest work scheduled first; big compressed logs
    staged plain and scrubbed across the --jobs pool; archives
    extracted through xz -T0, pigz or pbzip2 when present; pre-scans
    read in segments
  + Worker processes no longer duplicate log lines

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Jul 22 00:00:00 UTC 2026 - Ronald Pina <rpina@suse.com>

- Update to version 1.6
  + Performance: --jobs N process-parallel scrubbing; parallel IP learn
    pre-pass; large files scrubbed in line-aligned chunks; trie-regex
    keyword/serial passes; indexed IP lookup; parallel xz repack;
    verify now uses worker processes instead of GIL-bound threads
  + New --unpacked: leave scrubbed output fully unpacked, write
    compressed files back plain, skip the repack
  + New --profile: per-scrubber timing breakdown
  + Verbose: live phase times, slowest files, and a performance table
    with peak memory under --verbose
  + Inputs: scrub a mix of supportconfigs, crm/hb reports (incl
    .tar.bz2), folders, and plain files in one run with shared mappings
  + Nested tar archives unpacked recursively and scrubbed in place
  + Single-file compressed logs (.gz/.xz/.bz2) scrubbed instead of
    passed through as raw bytes
  + SAP: scrub SAP System IDs (usr/sap, sapmnt, rsc_SAP_<SID>,
    SAPSYSTEMNAME, <sid>adm)
  + Hostname: case-insensitive matching across underscore and digit
    boundaries; learn internal-TLD domains from hosts/resolv.conf;
    never auto-learn product-default container names (uyuni family);
    hostname_preserve config option
  + Hostname: scrub domain part of FQDN hostnames in output archive
    and folder names; rename hostname-bearing paths and file names
  + Email scrubber runs before hostname/domain so local parts do not
    survive; ssh public key user@host comments scrubbed
  + IP: contiguous netmasks left alone; IPv6 glued to a bare port
    matched; own fake output never re-scrubbed
  + Serial: short punctuation placeholders no longer obfuscated
  + Verify: no longer flags the tool's own deterministic hex fakes or
    dotted version strings the scrubber deliberately left alone
  + Extract: strip only a genuine single wrapper directory, never
    flatten multi-root archives
  + Output naming standardized as a frozen contract (docs + tests)
  + Default: private IP addresses left unobfuscated unless enabled
  + bin: self-locate the package from a git checkout, no PYTHONPATH

